<task id="on_the_sms_web_application_6" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>On the SMS web application</title>
   <shortdesc>To view parameter data:</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>Select</keyword>
        <keyword>placeholder</keyword>
        <keyword>parameter</keyword>
        <keyword>Parameters</keyword>
        <keyword>displayed</keyword>
        <keyword>click</keyword>
        <indexterm>Select</indexterm>
        <indexterm>placeholder</indexterm>
        <indexterm>parameter</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <taskbody>
      <context>
         <p>To view parameter data:</p>
      </context>
      <steps id="steps_10314146">
         <step>
            <cmd>Log in to the SMS web application.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select a motor on the <xref href="../dashboard/search_for_a_motor.dita" format="dita">left navigation pane</xref> or on the <xref href="../dashboard/monitor_motor_condition_list_view.dita" format="dita">List view</xref> to display the motor’s information page.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select the History plot tab.</cmd>
            <info>
               <p>The Parameters sub-tab is selected by default.</p>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select a parameter from the Motor parameters data drop-down list.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>Parameters sub-tab - Options</title>
                  <image height="308" href="../media/image45.png" placement="break" width="602">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select a date from the Date field.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select a time range from the Time range field.</cmd>
            <info>
               <p>The corresponding waveform is displayed.</p>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>To switch from one sample to another, click the different times the data was collected, below the horizontal axis.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>placeholder</title>
                  <image height="311" href="../media/image46.png" placement="break" width="602">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
               <p>Figure  Waveform displayed with different times</p>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>To zoom in on a specific time period, click and drag your mouse over the required dots. To zoom out, click Reset zoom on the bottom right of the page.</cmd>
            <info>
               <note type="note">Note: Hover over a specific dot to view exact readings.</note>
               <fig>
                  <title>placeholder</title>
                  <image height="316" href="../media/image47.png" placement="break" width="602">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
               <p>Figure  Waveform - zoomed in</p>
               <p>For more information on analyzing each parameter, see section <b>Sensor Information and Specifications</b> in the Analytics User Guide.</p>
               <p>To download parameter data:</p>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click DATA DOWNLOAD on the top right of the Parameters sub-tab.</cmd>
            <info>
               <p>The <b>Parameters Data Downloading</b> window is displayed.</p>
               <fig>
                  <title>Parameters Data Downloading window</title>
                  <image height="225" href="../media/image48.png" placement="break" width="433">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Confirm the date and time range, and the selected parameter or modify these details, as required.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Specify a file name.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click QUERY.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select the displayed time index and click GO.</cmd>
         </step>
      </steps>
      <result>
         <p>The data is downloaded to the specified file on your computer.</p>
      </result>
   </taskbody>
</task>
